# Development scratch for the working copy.
#
# This repository is the WORKSHOP: it carries the per-task development
# history. The published history lives in the GitHub clone, which receives
# one clean commit per release.

# Subagent-driven-development workspace: ledgers, briefs, review packages.
.superpowers/

# Build output. build-zip.ps1 writes one level up, but keep this in case
# someone runs it from here.
*.zip

# Composer-installed PHPCS toolchain. The lock file and composer.json are
# tracked deliberately; only the installed tree is ignored.
#
# The leading slash matters. Written as "vendor/" the rule matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, so it also covered assets/vendor/ -
# the bundled Chart.js and its date adapter, which DO ship in the plugin
# ZIP. Those two files were committed before the rule existed and stayed
# tracked (.gitignore does not apply to tracked files), so nothing was
# ever missing from a clone. But the next file added there would have
# been dropped without a word.
/vendor/

# Editor and OS clutter
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
